# What never enters the build context.
#
# Two reasons. A smaller context is a faster build, but the important one is
# that anything sent here can end up in a layer, and a layer is readable by
# anyone who can pull the image. The safe default is to send only what the
# build needs.

# Local secrets and environment files (SPECIFICATIONS.md section 31). The
# build needs no credential and is given none.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Build output: rebuilt inside the image, and a stale copy here would be
# sent over the wire for nothing. This directory is the largest thing in
# the repository by far.
target/

# Integration tests and their fixtures. The image ships a binary; these run
# in CI. Cargo discovers tests/ automatically, so leaving it out costs the
# build nothing.
#
# benches/ is deliberately NOT excluded: Cargo.toml declares the two
# benchmarks as explicit targets, and Cargo refuses to parse a manifest
# whose declared target files are missing, so excluding them breaks the
# build rather than shrinking it.
tests/

# Documentation and editor state.
*.md
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
